# What a group's header's OWN code is held to: the diagnostics of the region
# its include stands in (design.md §4.19, §1.12; panel 205's R2, ratified
# 2026-10-10; defect 569).
#
# **A header's own code was judged by where it was found.** clang quiets
# every warning located in a header it finds in a system directory, whatever
# `-I` says (GCC's and clang's documentation), so on Linux arm64 `gmp.h` in
# `/usr/include` built and printed `6`, while on this Mac the same program,
# `gmp.h` found under Homebrew through pkg-config's `-I`, was refused by
# `-Werror=sign-conversion` at `gmp.h:1882`, inside the library's own inline
# code, before any binding was checked; libavutil, avcodec, avformat,
# swscale and libfdt alike. And an environment variable decided it on one
# machine: `CPATH` refused it, `C_INCLUDE_PATH` (a system directory to
# clang) built it.
#
# **So the region is judged as one policy, wherever the header was found**:
# the diagnostic state is pushed, `-Wall` and `-Wsign-conversion` are
# ignored, the two families a library's own style trips, and the warnings
# that say the header's code the program RUNS has no defined behaviour, a
# missing return, a read of an uninitialised value, a `printf` whose
# arguments its format does not match, stay errors (`KEPT`, which `-Wall`'s
# ignore would otherwise take); `-Wshorten-64-to-32`, the pointer
# types and clang's default errors are not in `-Wall` and stay as the build's
# flags set them. The region is popped at the guard's close, and every check
# of a binding is raised again after it (`emit/checks_raised.hero`, defect
# 570), so nothing a header's code is excused from reaches a line the
# compiler wrote. Measured at the landing, 2026-10-10: the six libraries
# build on this Mac, `CPATH` and `C_INCLUDE_PATH` agree, a header of the
# program's own with a missing return, an uninitialised read or a 64-to-32
# narrowing is refused; panel 204's 182 Mac headers read 10 refusals and 0
# raw warnings where they read 16 and 2, exactly the six moving, and the 85
# Linux arm64 headers copied to a directory of the user's 2 where they read
# 3, `gmp.h` moving; and of the 1,456 tracked files with an `extern`, no
# program moved but the defect's own cases.
#
# **`-Wformat` is kept since 2026-10-10, after the landing** (the lane's
# question, the coordinator's ruling by the batch's standing default): the
# ratified region ignored it with the rest of `-Wall`, so a header's
# `printf("%d\n", "seven")` built and printed a pointer's low bits at exit 0.
# Kept, panel 204's 182 Mac headers read the same 10 refusals and 0 raw
# warnings header by header, measured that morning beside the landing. The
# repair was written at 2067ec87 on a branch never merged and landed with
# defect 2034, 2026-10-12, which found it unmerged.
#
# **Kept as a group, it refused what C defines** (defect 2036, 2026-10-13):
# a pragma on a group reaches each of its parts, so a header's
# `printf("%d\n", 7, 8)` was refused for `-Wformat-extra-args` and its
# `printf(m)` for `-Wformat-security`, and on Linux its `snprintf` cut at its
# size for `-Wformat-truncation`. A pragma on a part written after the one on
# its group decides that part, so the parts whose construct C defines are
# passed over after `KEPT`, as `-Wall` is (`FORMAT_DEFINED`), and the rest of
# the group stays an error.
#
# **A call to a function nobody declared went with `-Wall`** (defect 2052,
# 2026-10-13): `-Wimplicit-function-declaration` is one of `-Wall`'s, so the
# region's ignore turned clang's default error off, and a header's
# `(int)hero_str_le(8)` built as a call to a function C11 has no declaration
# of (6.5.1p2: an identifier is an expression only where it is declared),
# its result read as an `int` nobody promised; the link then stopped at
# exit 2, `internal error: linking failed`. A function of C's library the
# header never included, `abs(-8)` with no `<stdlib.h>`, built and printed 8
# at exit 0, clang declaring it itself. Kept, the header is refused at the
# call's line before any link, as the program's own lines are; of the 1,576
# tracked programs with an `extern`, none moved (measured at the repair).

use emit/checks_raised

# What a header's own code is not held to.
constant QUIETED: [str]
    [
        "-Wall"
        "-Wsign-conversion"
    ]

# What it still is, which `-Wall`'s ignore would otherwise turn off: each an
# error on the build's command line too, by `cli/flags.hero` or by clang's
# own default (`emit/checks_raised.hero`'s `DEFAULT_ERRORS`).
constant KEPT: [str]
    [
        "-Wreturn-type"
        "-Wuninitialized"
        "-Wformat"
        "-Wconditional-uninitialized"
        "-Wimplicit-function-declaration"
    ]

# The parts of `-Wformat` whose construct C defines, passed over after `KEPT`
# raised the group (defect 2036). The parts are clang's own: `diagtool tree
# -Wformat` of clang 22.1.8 lists nine, and clang 18.1.3's
# `DiagnosticGroups.td`, the floor's, the same nine. Each is here, or kept, for
# its construct:
#
# - `-Wformat-extra-args`, an argument past the format's last conversion:
#   C11 7.21.6.1p2 evaluates it and otherwise ignores it;
# - `-Wformat-zero-length`, an empty format handed an argument: the same
#   paragraph, every argument an excess one;
# - `-Wformat-security`, a format that is no literal and takes no argument:
#   C defines the call for whatever string it holds, which clang cannot see;
#   a literal is still judged whole;
# - `-Wformat-truncation`, with its `-non-kprintf` part, `snprintf` handed
#   less room than its output: 7.21.6.5p2 writes the first n-1 characters and
#   returns how many the whole would take; told by glibc's headers, never by
#   this Mac's, whose `snprintf` clang does not judge;
# - `-Wformat-y2k`, which holds no diagnostic in clang: GCC's, a `strftime`
#   format giving a two-digit year, is defined.
#
# Kept, by the same reading: `-Wformat-insufficient-args` (p2, too few
# arguments), `-Wformat-invalid-specifier` (p9, an invalid conversion),
# `-Wformat-overflow` (`sprintf` written past its array), `-Wnonnull` (a null
# where the declaration forbids one; 7.1.4p1 for the library's own), and the
# diagnostics the group holds itself, a conversion its argument does not
# match first among them (p9). **No pragma reaches one of those alone**, so a
# few constructs C defines are refused with them, measured on this Mac and
# Linux arm64: a flag p6 says is ignored (`%+ d`, `%-05d`), a `bool` for
# `%c`, a `\0` inside the format, a wide literal cast to `const char *`.
# **They stay refused, a known cost by the author's ruling of 2026-10-13**:
# robustness first (design.md §1.12), since passing them over would pass the
# mismatch that reads the wrong bytes; revisit if clang gives them a flag of
# their own. Each is pinned by a case of `tests/golden/unsupported/` named
# `fixedbugs-2036-...-is-a-known-cost`, which moves when it can be passed.
constant FORMAT_DEFINED: [str]
    [
        "-Wformat-extra-args"
        "-Wformat-zero-length"
        "-Wformat-security"
        "-Wformat-truncation"
        "-Wformat-y2k"
    ]

# The lines before the groups' includes: the push, the ignores, the kept,
# then the parts of a kept group passed over again.
function opening() -> [str]
    out: [str] @= ["#pragma clang diagnostic push"]

    for word in QUIETED
        out @ out.push("#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"" + word + "\"")

    for word in KEPT
        out @ out.push("#pragma clang diagnostic error \"" + word + "\"")

    for word in FORMAT_DEFINED
        out @ out.push("#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"" + word + "\"")

    return out

# The line after the guard's close, which gives back the state before the
# region; a header's own push left open is what the checks raised after it
# answer.
constant CLOSING: str
    "#pragma clang diagnostic pop"

## Tests

test "a header's own code is quiet of -Wall and sign conversion alone, a missing return, an uninitialised read and a mismatched format kept"
    got = opening()
    assert got[0] == "#pragma clang diagnostic push"
    assert got[1] == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wall\""
    assert got[2] == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wsign-conversion\""
    assert got[3] == "#pragma clang diagnostic error \"-Wreturn-type\""
    assert got[5] == "#pragma clang diagnostic error \"-Wformat\""
    assert got[7] == "#pragma clang diagnostic error \"-Wimplicit-function-declaration\""
    assert got.len() == 1 + QUIETED.len() + KEPT.len() + FORMAT_DEFINED.len()

    # A part of `-Wformat` C defines is passed over after the group is raised,
    # since the later pragma decides the part (defect 2036); written before
    # it, the group's `error` would take it back.
    index: i64 @= 1 + QUIETED.len() + KEPT.len()

    for part in FORMAT_DEFINED
        assert got[index] == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"" + part + "\""
        index @ index + 1

    # Each kept warning is a check the build raises after the region too.
    for word in KEPT
        found: bool @= false

        for one in checks_raised.checked()
            if one == word
                found @ true

        assert found
